-- Schedule (separate file): PROPOSED_20261004151000_market_intel_rollup_schedule.sql
-- =============================================================================
--
-- WHAT
--   Source of truth stays public.mv_map_market_sales. The summary is a versioned
--   projection written in BUILDS. Readers only ever see the latest build whose
--   status = 'ready', so a build in progress or a failed build is never served.
--   The previous ready build is kept, so going back is one UPDATE.
--     mi_rollup_builds           one row per build: status, cursor, units, fingerprint, timings,
--                                and the freshness the UI shows ("data as of")
--     mi_rollup_sync_state       last tick / skip reason (campaign-graph convention)
--     mi_asset_type_map          raw property_type → base class (parity-tested against JS)
--     mi_zip_geo                 per build: ZIP → state, city, county (+ how), market, sales, bounds
--     mi_geo_period_rollup       per build: geography × period × asset; counts + EXACT medians
--     mi_geo_month_rollup        per build: geography × month × asset; trends, coverage, growth
--     mi_buyer_activity          per build: the ~12.7K sales with a named company buyer
--                                (privacy and lender rules stay in JS: buyer-name-privacy.js /
--                                buyer-identity-rules.js)
--
-- EXACT, NOT APPROXIMATE
--   Every median is percentile_cont(0.5) over the qualified rows of exactly that
--   (geography, period, asset) group, recomputed from raw sales each build. Medians are
--   never averaged or merged from smaller groups. Price deciles use percentile_disc.
--   Windows end at the build's source as-of (max sold_on) and are the same day counts as
--   the API (30/90/182/365/1095 days, all).
--
-- INCREMENTAL / NIGHTLY (campaign-graph conventions)
--   - mi_rollup_tick() does ONE unit per call: an advisory lock, the load guard
--     (> 12 active client backends or a query running > 10 s → skip), a cursor in
--     mi_rollup_builds, and a 30 s statement cap set by the cron command.
--   - Units: prepare · buyers · 36 period units (6 periods × 6 levels, ordered period by period) ·
--     6 month units · finalize · 3 cleanup.
--     Measured ≤ 10 s each, read side, on prod (see the plan doc).
--   - Nightly: a build starts only if the source fingerprint changed (row count, sum of
--     prices, first/last sale, membership, census) or the last build is older than 7 days.
--     Unchanged means one fingerprint scan a night and nothing written.
--   - Cold-cache tolerant: a unit that errors or hits the cap is rolled back alone
--     (sub-transaction), recorded, and retried on the next tick. After 3 failures the
--     build is marked failed; readers keep the previous ready build.
--   - finalize re-checks the fingerprint. If the MV changed mid-build, the build fails
--     and the next tick starts a fresh one; never a mixed build.
--
-- SECURITY: tables, the view and functions are service_role-only (revoked from PUBLIC,
